<section class="nfb _hs1" aria-labelledby="bitc-h1">
 {%- comment -%}
 Full-bleed photograph, the manual's 70% layout. Point the metafield
 `page.metafields.custom.hero_image` at the frame, or replace the <img> here.
 A Carbon scrim — never a red wash — keeps the white copy above 4.5:1.
 {%- endcomment -%}
 <div class="_hero">
 {%- comment -%}
 The hero film is decoration, not content: muted, looping, no controls, and it never
 carries meaning the copy does not. `playsinline` keeps iOS from taking it fullscreen,
 `preload=metadata` keeps the first paint cheap, and a visitor who asked their system
 for less motion gets the still frame instead — the CSS stops it and shows the poster.
 {%- endcomment -%}
 {%- assign bitc_hero = page.metafields.custom.hero_image -%}
