{%- comment -%}
 ── Configuration ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 BITC_BLOG handle of the blog that carries the series. Used when the page is not
 a blog template (the hub is a normal page and has no `blog` object).
 The live store's general blog is `novinky`; the series gets its own blog
 because a Liquid loop over `blog.articles` stops at the newest 50, and
 Novinky already holds ~25 material entries and keeps growing — chapter
 articles would eventually fall out of the hub's reach.
 BITC_SERIES series tag, used only when the series shares a blog with other content.
 Leave empty when the series has its own blog (the recommended setup).
 CH_TAGS chapter tags, in order. An article belongs to a chapter by carrying its
 tag; a chapter with no published article renders as "coming soon".
 CH_NAMES chapter names. Proper names and product lines stay in English in every
 market (Katka, Peak Flow); only the subtitles are translated (t_chNsub).
 PER cards per page in the archive grid.
 FILMS the HERO episodes: `YouTubeID|Title|Duration|Blurb`, films separated by `;;`
 because a blurb may contain a comma. The page
 shows the YouTube thumbnail and only loads the player after a click, so an
 unwatched film costs the visitor nothing. Empty list → empty slots, which is
 what the page should say while the films are still being cut.
 SHORTS YouTube Shorts IDs, comma separated. Same click-to-play rule.
 AV_MARKETS markets that get the films and shorts, comma separated. Empty means every
 market: the films are spoken in Slovak, but YouTube offers the viewer
 auto-translated captions in the player, so a German or Bulgarian visitor can
 follow them. Fill it in (e.g. 'sk') to narrow the blocks to one market.
 FULL_FILM YouTube id of the full cut — all three episodes in one — linked under them.
 HERO_VIDEO looping background film for the hero. Empty → grey placeholder.
 SHOP_URL where the shoes live — the button under the product row.
 SHOP_COLLECTION handle of the collection the product rows are pulled from.
 SHOP_COUNT how many products to show — 8 fills two rows of four.
 HUB_ARTICLES article handles shown under the films, in this order. A handle that
 does not resolve is skipped, so a renamed article cannot break the page.
 FEATURED article handles, in the order they should appear at the top. Shopify orders
 a blog by publish date only, so an import buried the editorial writing under
 eighty material entries. This list is read by handle, so it reaches an
 article at any depth — a tag would only reach the newest fifty — and the
 order is exactly the order written here. The first four fill the band; the
 rest open the grid on page one. An unknown handle is skipped in silence.
 SHOW_READ_TIME off while most articles keep their text in an EComposer template
 rather than in `article.content` — the number would be missing on some
 cards and present on others. Turn it on once the bodies or the
 `read_time` metafields are filled in.
 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
